                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_214\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit modifies TransfersTableAdapter.java by removing the use of\n`java.util.Currency` / `java.text.NumberFormat` (specifically\n`Currency.getInstance(smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol())` combined with\n`Helper.newCurrencyFormat(getContext(), currency, locale)`), and restores the\nsimpler, previously-working approach:\n`String fiatSymbol = Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol(smartcoinAmount.getAsset());`\n`String eqValue = String.format(\"~ %s %.2f\", fiatSymbol, Util.fromBase(smartcoinAmount));`\nIt also removes the `Locale` constructor parameter added to\n`TransfersTableAdapter` and the corresponding call site in\n`BalancesFragment.java`, reverting to the two-argument constructor.\n\nExamining the candidates, candidate_213 has the original, correct code using\n`Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol(...)` (matching what the fix restores). The very\nnext relevant change, candidate_214, is the one that introduces the buggy\npattern the fix later removes:\n- It adds `import java.util.Currency;` and `import java.text.NumberFormat;`\n  to TransfersTableAdapter.java.\n- It comments out the previously working\n  `Helper.fetchStringSharePref(...)` / `new Locale(language)` lines inside\n  `renderAmount`, and instead adds a `Locale locale` field populated via a new\n  constructor parameter.\n- Critically, it replaces the safe `Smartcoins.getFiatSymbol(...)` call with\n  `Currency.getInstance(smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol())`. Smartcoin\n  asset symbols in this codebase (e.g. \"bitUSD\", \"bitCNY\", or other\n  BitShares-specific smartcoin symbols) are not valid ISO 4217 currency\n  codes, so `Currency.getInstance()` throws an `IllegalArgumentException`\n  for any symbol that isn't a real-world currency code, crashing the\n  transfers table rendering \u2014 this is the bug the fix commit addresses.\n- It also updates `BalancesFragment.java` to call the new\n  `TransfersTableAdapter(getContext(), locale, account, ...)` constructor,\n  which is exactly the call site the fix commit reverts back to the\n  three-argument version.\n\nSince candidate_214 is the first commit to introduce the\n`Currency.getInstance(smartcoinAmount.getAsset().getSymbol())` /\n`Helper.newCurrencyFormat` logic (which the fix commit directly reverts) and\nno earlier candidate contains this pattern, candidate_214 is the\nbug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
              }
